      "math_academy_id": "e-4820",
      "problem": "Given that  ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14122164/assets/ec6ac8b33e5df7d49042e6b2c671ea637690ef5ff9fc3e76a250463c0f6ce1e6.svg) find a basis for $\\textrm{Null}(A).$",
      "worked_solution": "Any vector in $\\textrm{Null}(A)$ has the form\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14122164/assets/1b6e7f7c8a685170ca348eec68c65f188714cd29b05dad54dabef303433b6e12.svg)\n\nExpanding, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3}-{x}_{4} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{4} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{4}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a basis for $\\textrm{Null}(A)$ is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14122164/assets/d7dd8080d1ac0d2380c6681b0fd23383432d3124b39a6c88be75baa34ec50262.svg)\n\nsince it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\textrm{Null}(A).$",
